# question: If a clinician is concerned about a patient's organ, which alarms would be relevant?
# rationale: Combines a diagnostic route (metric -> physiological property ->
#   process -> organ) and a therapeutic route (administered therapy ->
#   targeted process -> organ) to find every organ an alarm is relevant to,
#   including alarms with no measurement at all.
#
# reasoning: required
#
# Two independent routes to an organ, either one suffices:
#
#   diagnostic   the alarm's OWN metric -approximates-> property
#                -isPropertyOf-> process -presentIn-> organ
#   therapeutic  the device -administers-> therapy -targetsProcess-> process
#                -presentIn-> organ (no metric needed: a ventilator
#                disconnect is relevant to the lungs)
#
# Own metric only: the metric reached through any number of derivation
# steps that no further step consumes (build_framework.py
# derivation_graph(), 2026-11-24). An intermediate metric's organ does NOT
# count: an SVR alarm reports vascular resistance, not the cardiac output it
# is computed from, so it is relevant to the blood vessels and not, through
# that input, to the heart (decided in the CQ review of 2026-11-25; the old
# fixed tail .../analyzedBy/producesMetric stopped at the FIRST metric of a
# chain and so did the opposite). Which metrics an alarm depends on is a
# dependency question, CQ6's, not this one.
#
# Deliberate asymmetry: organ relevance comes from what is measured or
# what is administered, not from what a device could have measured. A
# therapy-device fault reaches its organ through the therapy route, but a
# monitoring-loss alarm (e.g. "Monitor - SpO2 sensor uit", "PHILIPSMONITOR -
# ECG alle leads los", a signal-quality fault) has no metric and administers
# nothing, so it reaches no organ: losing observation of an organ is not an
# effect on it. Broadening this (functional unit -> the metrics it can
# produce -> organ) was considered and rejected in the 2026-11-25 review.
#
# Metrics without a diagnostic route, at p75: VentilationCircuitLeak and
# DeliveredVolume (equipment quantities, no physiological property),
# Humidity (property without a process) and AirTemperature (no property).
# None loses an organ by it: all sit on a ventilator or incubator and reach
# Lungs or Skin through the therapeutic route.
#
# Validated 2026-11-25 on p75 (Lungs 51, Heart 19, Skin 18, BloodVessels 11,
# Kidneys 1 alarm types): every physiological alarm reaches an organ.
# Own-metric vs. first-metric scope makes no difference at p75 (no derived
# metrics); at p99 it removes 10 (alarm, organ) pairs, all EDWARDS
# (SVR/SVRI -> Heart, EDV/EDVI/SVI -> BloodVessels).

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>

SELECT ?organ (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?label; separator=" | ") AS ?alarms)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?a) AS ?matchCount) WHERE {
  ?a a mda:AlarmType ; mda:hasLabel ?label ; mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy ?dev .
  {
    ?dev mda:hasFunctionalUnit/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/(mda:producesSignal|mda:producesMetric))*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metricNode .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?metricNode mda:analyzedBy ?consumer }
    ?metricNode mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf/mda:presentIn ?organ .
  } UNION {
    ?dev mda:administers/mda:targetsProcess/mda:presentIn ?organ .
  }
}
GROUP BY ?organ
ORDER BY ?organ
